WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.670
Here's an interesting media story. Another
Fox news reporter has quit. So we had Shepard

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:09.749
Smith quitting a few weeks ago. This time
it's Catherine Herridge, who certainly much

00:00:09.749 --> 00:00:16.250
less well known than Shep Smith. Catherine
Herridge known more for holding up documents

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:22.430
in front of the camera. During her reports,
she has quit Fox news. And what's really funny

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:28.210
is that there are conflicting reports. She
used the term facts matter. She used it in

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:33.309
a statement that was released by her outgoing
employer, Fox news, and she used the term

00:00:33.309 --> 00:00:39.190
facts matter in a statement by her new upcoming
employer, CBS news. She's going from Fox news

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:44.749
to CBS news. But what's very interesting is
that depending on which of the two statements

00:00:44.749 --> 00:00:53.089
you read, the interpretation of facts matter
either can appear to be praise for Fox news

00:00:53.089 --> 00:00:55.640
or an attack against Fox news.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:01:00.430
Take a look at the two statements. So the
statement released via Fox news was, I have

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:04.739
received great personal satisfaction from
mentoring the next generation of reporters

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:10.600
and producers and sharing my journalistic
values that facts matter and enterprise reporting

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:16.350
will always win the day. This one seems to
imply that at Fox news she was able to share

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:22.650
her value that facts matter. Now when you
look at the CBS news statement from Catherine

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:29.280
Herridge, CBS news has always placed a premium
on enterprise journalism and powerful investigations.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:34.840
I feel privileged to join a team where facts
and storytelling will always matter. Which

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:39.770
of course the second one is sort of suggesting
that at CBS news, facts always matter. But

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:44.820
where she's coming from at Fox news facts
did not always matter, which of course we

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:51.260
know now as far as Catherine heritage is concerned,
even if this is her taking a stand against

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:54.440
the propaganda echo chamber of Fox where facts
don't matter.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.920
I mean, if she's not necessarily saying it,
I will. And most of you know that facts do

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:04.620
not matter at Fox news. I have a hard time
feeling super proud of this stand that she's

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:09.679
taking, if it is indeed what she's doing.
She's been there for a very long time. Nothing

00:02:09.679 --> 00:02:15.580
has actually changed now on Fox news where
now it's clearly the right thing to do if

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:20.340
you care about facts to quit. But at some
point in the past, if you cared about facts,

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:25.150
it was okay to be at Fox news. And she's also
not a particularly recognizable face there

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:31.550
anyways. So I, I'm not going to, uh, you know,
make any, uh, positive, uh, assessments of

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:37.901
what she's doing here. But the interesting
story is a broader one about some of the Fox

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:43.010
news departures of the last couple of years.
So we had Megan Kelly starting sometime back

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:47.230
after a very public sort of dispute with then
candidate Trump.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:52.530
Uh, we had Shep Smith more recently and then
you know, some smaller contributors like Catherine

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:57.540
Herridge who have just more quietly disappeared
from Fox news. But in the end, and this is

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:03.849
really the big story, Fox is still crushing
the ratings. There are some concerning numbers

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:09.150
that I'll tell you about in a moment, but
Fox news is still widely dominating the cable

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:16.660
news ratings. Now there's an argument to be
made that Fox news is the place for a particular

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:23.340
type of audience and therefore they're sort
of coalescing audiences that on the other

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:28.480
side are kind of split between a broader variety
of news outlets. That's the Madoff mathematical

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:32.790
argument, but you can't deny that they're
still widely crushing the ratings, the one

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:38.130
area where Fox is not doing so well. And this
may be interesting upcoming as we get into

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:44.670
the 2020 election. Adults 25 to 54 are considered
like the important demographic in the news

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:45.670
world.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:51.870
Sometimes they're referred to as the demo,
the demographic that matters, foxes down 5%

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:58.491
in total primetime viewers this past October
compared to the previous October of 2018 they're

00:03:58.491 --> 00:04:06.860
down 13% in total day viewers, they're down
25% in the primetime key demographic that

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:15.120
we're talking about, age 25 to 54 and they
are down 27% in the total day demographic

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:20.900
of adults, 25 to 54 so Fox is doing well,
they're beating out CNN, they're beating out

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:26.970
MSNBC at, at all, most, if not all times of
the day across the spectrum. But they are

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:33.900
having a growing problem with this important
key demographic of adults 25 to 54 now, fortunately

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:38.650
for them, them, it doesn't really matter,
right? They don't need to be profitable since

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:42.770
they have these rich right-wingers that fund
them. And that's going to continue, I won't

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:46.960
say in perpetuity because nothing lasts forever,
particularly in media, but for the foreseeable

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:47.990
future.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:53.540
But this also connects to 2020 and it also
connects to the, the growing sort of rift

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:58.710
between Donald Trump and Fox news. On the
one hand, you have the folks like, you know,

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:04.479
Sean Hannity and Janine Pirro and I believe
Laura Ingram for the most part is on the Trump

00:05:04.479 --> 00:05:10.389
train. They are effectively Trump Brown nosers
a functioning almost as state media on Fox

00:05:10.389 --> 00:05:14.690
news on a daily basis. Jeanine Pirro on a
weekly basis, I think. But then you've got

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:19.620
people like Tucker Carlson who's not always
on the Trump train. You have Shep Smith, who

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:24.260
certainly wasn't and has now left. And Donald
Trump over the last year or 15 months as we've

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:29.900
been talking about, has been more and more
frequently promoting the even crazier alternative

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:35.940
to Fox news. Oh, a N or O a N N one American
news network. So this is going to be an interesting

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:38.310
media narrative heading into 2020.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:45.910
Now remember in 2016 really 2015 when Fox
news was not behind Donald Trump, they were

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:53.480
not behind Trump in a less overtly, uh, problematic
way for the right because there were all sorts

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:59.260
of more establishment Republicans that they
could support or be behind Ted Cruz or Jeb

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:04.080
Bush or whoever, until eventually they got
behind Donald Trump. As it became clear he

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:10.380
was going to be the nominee. This time there
is less sort of plausible reasoning for Fox

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:14.500
news or right wing echo chamber, not to be
behind Trump because there is at least as

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:18.139
of yet no serious primary challenger to Donald
Trump. And it doesn't appear that there's

00:06:18.139 --> 00:06:23.250
going to be one. So the circumstances would
be far different if Fox were not to be Holy

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:27.780
behind Trump as we get into the 2020 election.
I expect they will be, but I think there might

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:32.470
still be some interesting drama to be seen.
